 "findings": [
  "Converse replays the signed reasoning of every earlier assistant turn (276 replayed blocks in 24 requests on every arm), so after the first pass every later request carries invalidated blocks: carrier 17 of 24 requests, 214 block replays.",
  "The round-0 gate (v1) leaves Bedrock Converse unchanged (214 / 17), because it returns False unless api_mode is anthropic_messages.",
  "Gate v2 declines every fresh pass on this route: 0 passes, 0 invalidated replays.",
  "Every arm, including base, logs 2 blocked getaddrinfo('bedrock-runtime.us-east-1.amazonaws.com') before the endpoint override applies; all 24 requests reached the fake."
 ],
 "source_caveat": "The claude-api reference states the conversation check for the Messages API on every platform (Claude in Amazon Bedrock included) and lists the legacy Bedrock InvokeModel / Converse integration as out of its scope. Enforcement on Converse is assumed here from the shared signature mechanism, not documented in that reference.",
